⚙️ Ansible when Condition

In automation, not every task should run every time.
That is where the when condition is used.

🔹 What when does

 The when keyword tells Ansible to run a task only if a condition is true.
If the condition is false, the task is skipped.

🔹 Why when is important

 It allows playbooks to make decisions.
 It prevents unnecessary or incorrect changes.
 It helps the same playbook work across different systems.

🔹 Common use cases

 • Run tasks based on OS type
 • Execute actions only for specific environments
 • Skip tasks if a variable has a certain value
 • Apply configuration conditionally

🔹 How when works conceptually

 • Ansible evaluates the condition
 • If true, the task runs
 • If false, the task is skipped
No errors. Just a clean skip.

🔹 Simple mental model

 Tasks describe actions.
 when decides whether they apply.
